  "_field": "Each work carries a received_status. THE STATUS IS RECORDED, NOT ENDORSED.",
  "_note": "The genuine/spurious partition of this corpus is an inference, not an attestation. The corpus was constituted by Andronicus of Rhodes in the first century BCE — some 250 years after Aristotle — working, on the tradition's own account, from the cross-references the texts contain and from school documents. His catalogue is not extant. His judgments have been overturned: he held De interpretatione spurious, and the field now receives it as genuine. Metaphysics A was contested in antiquity and attributed by some to Pasicles of Rhodes. The criteria that produced the partition — internal consistency, style, doctrinal fit — are the same criteria whose circularity is at issue wherever authorship is the question. This seat therefore records the received status as a field to be tested against, not a filter to measure through. Any analysis that excludes the spuria to sharpen a result about Aristotle has used a category built from the consistency it is measuring.",
